    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d642">

                <pb facs="0731" n="417" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg417"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 165.102/284</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-12-08T19:00:00+01:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">December 8, 1914, 7 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 9, 8 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>1036. Informed that one month’s supply of dyestuffs has been released for the
                    shipment by German authorities and that shipment was started for Rotterdam
                    yesterday. Shipment to be made on <hi rendition="#italic">Matanzas</hi> and is
                    to be of about 2,200 tons, practically filling steamer. Further release will be
                    made of amount of dyes damaged on <hi rendition="#italic">Sun</hi> as soon as
                    this amount is established. No further release for any period until present
                    shipment has been used up.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
